config SERVICE_TOUCH
    bool "Touch"
    default y if TOUCH
    help
      Touch event service. Requires a touch driver (CONFIG_TOUCH).

if SERVICE_TOUCH

config TOUCH_NAV_BUTTONS
    bool "Synthesize navigation buttons from touch gestures"
    default n
    help
      Translate touchscreen gestures into synthetic Pebble button events so the
      button-driven UI can be navigated by touch on devices with fewer than the
      four buttons PebbleOS assumes: swipe up/down -> UP/DOWN (scroll menus),
      tap -> SELECT (activate). The synthetic events are injected into the normal
      kernel button pipeline, so the launcher, menus and watchface all respond
      without any app-level changes. Intended for boards with a touchscreen but
      a reduced button count (e.g. Bangle.js 2).

config TOUCH_WIDGET_DRAG
    bool "Drag-to-scroll widgets on touch boards"
    default n
    depends on TOUCH
    help
      Auto-attach a vertical drag recognizer to ScrollLayer so its content
      offset tracks a touch drag directly, instead of going through
      synthesized navigation buttons. Deliberately decoupled from
      TOUCH_NAV_BUTTONS: a board can drag-scroll widgets with or without
      synthetic button emulation.
      MenuLayer reconciles its selection against a drag-moved content
      offset: if the selected row scrolls out of view during an actual
      finger drag, selection moves to the nearest row still visible, the
      highlight is repositioned to match, and any stale selection
      animation left over from a synthesized button click is cancelled --
      so a tap after dragging a menu activates the row the user actually
      sees selected. Reconciliation is scoped to real drags only: it does
      not run for animated or unanimated programmatic scrolls (e.g.
      menu_layer_set_selected_index()), which are left alone.
      Notably not reconciled: (1) while a center-focused MenuLayer's own
      selection-change animation is in flight, dragging moves the content
      offset but the selection is left as-is until that animation
      finishes; reconciliation resumes normally afterward. (2) if no row
      overlaps the newly visible band (e.g. it contains only a section
      header), the selection is left off-screen with no highlight move
      and no selection-changed callback.

module = SERVICE_TOUCH
module-str = Touch
source "src/fw/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif
